 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Eating out in Melbourne cost more in August 2026 than a year earlier, and the annual rate of increase has risen over the past 18 months or so.\n\n**Melbourne, annual change in the CPI (August 2026)**\n- Meals out and takeaway foods rose 3.5%.\n- Restaurant meals rose 3.3%.\n- All groups CPI rose 3.5%, so eating out is rising at about the same pace as prices overall.\n\n**How the pace has changed**\n- Meals out and takeaway in Melbourne was up 2.6% in April 2025.\n- It reached 3.5% by October 2025.\n- It peaked at 4.4% in May 2026.\n- It has eased to 4.1% in July and 3.5% in August 2026.\n- Restaurant meals followed a similar path, from 2.5% in April 2025 to a peak of 4.1% in May 2026, then 3.9% in July and 3.3% in August 2026.\n\n**Melbourne compared with Australia (August 2026)**\n- Nationally, meals out and takeaway rose 4.1% and restaurant meals rose 4.3%.\n- Melbourne's rises are smaller than the national figures.\n- Overall CPI was 3.5% in Melbourne against 4.0% nationally.\n\nThese are year-on-year changes in the original (not seasonally adjusted) series.",
